# Exit hand-back of the terminal: on quit the console gives mouse tracking
# and the extended key reporting back to the terminal — the shell it returns
# to must not inherit either (regression: after quit, the terminal was left
# in mouse-reporting mode, so the shell's wheel and clicks typed raw mouse
# bytes into the prompt and selection did not work).
#
#   bin/metatron-console --steps bin/test/console-exit-release.steps --raw raw.txt
#
# The release bytes themselves are verified against the raw transcript:
# the full mouse-off sweep (..1006l..1016l) and the extend-mode reset (>4;0m)
# must arrive, and nothing on the way out may re-arm an enable.

WAIT_CONSOLE

# a widget on screen keeps the pointer armed through the prompts — the quit
# is what has to take it to the terminal's own side
MARK quit
SEND :quit
WAIT shutdown 30
